Use io.
Define local values as array<whole number, 9>.
Set item 0 of values to 3.
Set item 1 of values to 4.
Set item 2 of values to 5.
Set item 3 of values to 6.
Set item 4 of values to 7.
Set item 5 of values to 8.
Set item 6 of values to 9.
Set item 7 of values to 10.
Set item 8 of values to 11.
Let checks be 0.
If every x in values is more than 0, add 1 to checks.
If some x in values is more than 10, add 2 to checks.
If no x in values is less than 0, add 4 to checks.
Say checks.
Give back 0.
